From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: tests: adapt upstream tests to the NixOS execution environment

The postprocessors intend to remove a symbol offset beginning with "+0x".
An unescaped leading plus is not a valid extended regular expression in
modern gawk, so the postprocessor itself fails before it can assess DTrace's
output.

The trampoline annotation test relies on BEGIN to terminate DTrace.  BEGIN can
fire before the later io trampoline has been emitted under slow emulation.  Use
the -c synchronization point instead: DTrace starts the child only after probe
enablement is complete, then exits when the child terminates.

The FBT stress tests intend to check entry and return arguments and a nested
call, but their empty function fields attach to every FBT probe in the kernel.
Contemporary generic kernels expose more than 150,000 such probes, turning
functional checks into accidental multi-gigabyte scalability tests.  Trace
vfs_read, which the DTrace consumer itself exercises, and its rw_verify_area
call.  This also ports the tail-call case away from the obsolete ioctl symbol.
Use a global readiness flag where the selected probe is independent of the
thread that delivered tick-1.

NixOS provides the iputils IPv6 implementation as `ping -6`, rather than the
legacy `ping6` alias.  Current kernels also expose the task_rename tracepoint's
pid argument, shifting the arguments asserted by the SDT test.

Keep cleanup diagnostics from a successfully completed NFS trace out of the
golden output, record the lockstat probes available on current aarch64 kernels,
and make the runtime lookup of the USDT test's temporary shared libraries
explicit.

diff --git a/test/unittest/ip/tst.ipv6localicmp.sh b/test/unittest/ip/tst.ipv6localicmp.sh
--- a/test/unittest/ip/tst.ipv6localicmp.sh
+++ b/test/unittest/ip/tst.ipv6localicmp.sh
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ local=::1
 # Check that we have an IPv6 local configuration to work with, or expect fail
 /sbin/ip -o route get to $local > /dev/null || exit 67
 
-$dtrace $dt_flags -c "ping6 -q $local -c 3" -qs /dev/stdin <<EOF | \
+$dtrace $dt_flags -c "ping -6 -q $local -c 3" -qs /dev/stdin <<EOF | \
     gawk '/ip::/ { print $0 }' | sort -n
 ip:::send
 /args[2]->ip_saddr == "$local" && args[2]->ip_daddr == "$local" &&
